      "text": [
        " اللَّهِ جَلَّ ثَنَاؤُهُ ثُمَّ لْيَقْضُوا تَفَثَهُمْ قَالَ هُوَ مَا يَكُونُ مِنَ الرَّجُلِ فِي إِحْرَامِهِ فَإِذَا دَخَلَ مَكَّةَ فَتَكَلَّمَ بِكَلَامٍ طَيِّبٍ كَانَ ذَلِكَ كَفَّارَةً لِذَلِكَ الَّذِي كَانَ مِنْهُ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Humeyd Bin Ziyad, from Ibn Sama’at, from someone else, from Aban, from Abu Baseer, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> regarding the Words of Allah<sup>azwj</sup>, Majestic is His<sup>azwj</sup> Praise <span class=\"ibTxt\"><a href=\"/#/books/quran:22#h29\"><a href=\"/books/quran:22#h29\">[22:29]</a></a> Then let them fulfil their needful acts</span>. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘It is what happens from the man who is in his <span class=\"iTxt\">Ihraam</span>. So when he enters Makkah, so he would speak with the good speech. That would be an expiation for that which was from him’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "15. Humayd ibn Ziyad has narrated from ibn Sama‘ah from more than one person from Aban from abu Basir who has said the following: “Abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said the following about the words of Allah, glorious is whose praise, ‘They should spruce up.’ He (the Imam) said that this is about what one may have had in the state of Ihram. When he enters Makkah, he should speak proper words and this will be considered as expiation for what he has had in the state of Ihram.’” "
        ]
      }
    },
